   "pass": true,
   "shownText": "[BW] Renal impairment is a risk factor for metformin-associated lactic acidosis. · [8.6] Metformin is kidney-excreted; accumulation and lactic acidosis risk increase with renal impairment, and use is contraindicated when eGFR is below 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2. · [2.3] Assess renal function before starting and periodically after starting metformin hydrochloride tablets. · [2.3] Starting metformin hydrochloride tablets is not recommended at eGFR 30 to 45 mL/minute/1.73 m 2; reassess continuation if eGFR falls below 45, and discontinue if it falls below 30."
